WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.737
The final coding exercise combines preservation, cardinality, and aggregation.

00:00:05.737 --> 00:00:11.702
The result must contain one row per department, including departments with zero activity.

00:00:11.702 --> 00:00:15.842
Start from departments because that is the population to preserve.

00:00:15.842 --> 00:00:21.232
LEFT JOIN admissions by department and LEFT JOIN medical staff by department.

00:00:21.232 --> 00:00:28.012
Because one department can have several admissions and several staff members, the combined rows can multiply.

00:00:28.012 --> 00:00:32.032
If you count rows directly, the measures may be inflated.

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:35.937
Use distinct identifiers when counting admissions and staff.

00:00:35.937 --> 00:00:41.162
Then GROUP BY department so the final grain is one department per row.

00:00:41.162 --> 00:00:45.257
After Run and Check, find the department with no activity.

00:00:45.257 --> 00:00:47.857
It should still appear with zero counts.

00:00:47.857 --> 00:00:53.537
Then inspect a busy department and make sure the counts reflect real admissions and real staff,

00:00:53.537 --> 00:00:56.287
not the multiplied join combinations.

00:00:56.287 --> 00:01:02.322
This is very similar to real management reporting where every region, team, program,

00:01:02.322 --> 00:01:06.160
or product category must appear even when activity is zero.
